course: dictionary
lesson: 9632
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word study can be a verb or a noun, and it can mean different things. As a verb, study means to spend time learning by reading, practising and thinking. «Rangers and scientists study droppings» means they look at them very carefully to learn things.
explain: As a noun, a study is a piece of research to find out facts. «A 2022 study estimated about 20 quadrillion ants on Earth» means scientists tested and counted to find an answer. A study can also be a quiet room in a house for reading, writing or working.
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the clues around the word. In «If a study shows red wins, how big was the difference?», a study shows results, so it means research. Try your meaning in the sentence, and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Study can be a verb (to study, studies, studied, studying) or a noun (a study, studies).
fact: To study means to spend time learning about something by reading, practising and thinking.
fact: A study is a piece of research to find out facts, like «a 2022 study».
fact: A study can also be a quiet room in a house for reading, writing or working.
fact: «Studies» can mean school subjects, like «social studies».
exercise: «In school, pupils study maths, science and history.» What does study mean here? | A kind of fruit | *To learn about something by reading and practising | A loud noise at night | A soft, comfy chair
exercise: «Rangers and scientists study droppings to learn which animals live in a place.» What does study mean here? | *To look at something very carefully | To cook a meal | To sell things in a shop | To sleep in a tent
exercise: «The rangers wrote a study about the frogs.» What does study mean here? | A school subject like art | *A piece of research to find out facts | A type of frog | A quiet room for reading
test: «Dan went to his study to finish his homework.» What is the study? | To learn by reading and practising | *A quiet room in a house for reading or working | A school subject like maths | A piece of research to find facts
test: Grace says she will «study hard» for her spelling test. What does study mean here? | To run very fast | *To spend time learning by reading and practising | To hide from the teacher | To paint a picture very carefully
exam: «If a study shows red wins, how big was the difference, and did anyone repeat it?» What meaning of study fits here? | *A piece of research that finds facts | A quiet room in a house | To learn by reading and practising | A school subject like maths
